From: KRdp displayless experiment <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Give the desktop to one remote seat at a time

Upstream places no limit on concurrent connections, and each one brings its own
virtual monitor, so a second client extends the desktop instead of taking it
over. Identical geometry merely confuses; differing geometry puts windows on one
monitor and leaves the other unreachable.

Close the incumbent when a new connection is activated. That is safe to do
bluntly only because 50becf4 gave the run thread sole ownership of the FreeRDP
peer: a streaming session now reaches Closed by itself, tears down, and releases
its output through the lifecycle hook. Before that fix this needed a deadline
and takeover state machine purely to work around sessions that never died.

diff --git a/server/SessionController.cpp b/server/SessionController.cpp
index 8f352ef..ff34b7a 100644
--- a/server/SessionController.cpp
+++ b/server/SessionController.cpp
@@ -248,6 +248,25 @@ void SessionController::onNewConnection(KRdp::RdpConnection *newConnection)
             return;
         }
 
+        // One remote seat. Upstream places no limit on concurrent connections
+        // and every one of them brings its own virtual monitor along, so a
+        // second client does not take the desktop over - it extends it. When
+        // the two ask for the same geometry that is merely confusing; when they
+        // differ, windows live on one monitor and the other is unreachable.
+        //
+        // Closing the incumbent bluntly is safe here only because upstream gave
+        // the run thread sole ownership of the FreeRDP peer (50becf4): a
+        // streaming session now reaches Closed on its own, tears down, and
+        // releases its output through the lifecycle hook. Before that fix this
+        // needed a whole deadline-and-takeover state machine to work around
+        // sessions that never died.
+        for (const auto &incumbent : m_wrappers) {
+            if (incumbent->connection && incumbent->connection != newConnection) {
+                qInfo() << "KRDP-SEAT: closing incumbent session" << incumbent->connection << "for" << newConnection;
+                incumbent->connection->close();
+            }
+        }
+
         auto wrapper = std::make_unique<SessionWrapper>(newConnection, makeSession(), m_sni);
